# The machine-local tiers. NO trailing slash on any of them, deliberately: a
# trailing slash means "directory only", and git treats a symlink as a blob, not
# a directory — so /output/ would NOT ignore output, which is a symlink into
# iCloud here. Untracked, it would offer git an absolute path naming one machine.
# Which tiers are symlinks is a per-machine fact (output is one here, input is
# not), so no slash on any: without one a rule ignores a directory AND a symlink,
# and stops depending on the shape a tier happens to have on whoever's disk.
/input
/cache
/output
/logs

**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# the machine binding: this machine names ITSELF here, and that name is never
# shared, never transported. It sits at the root beside the other machine-local
# entries above (cache/, input/, logs/, output/) because that is what it IS —
# not inside rsc/machine/, where its name keys a registry every clone shares.
/machine-name.txt
